Phew.....only took me about 6 months, but I finally ascended. Use Windows 
Nethack with the Absurd64 Tileset shrunk down to less-absurd 32. Previously 
used another tileset "tiles32" but found the Absurd one a few weeks ago, and 
after shrinking it, preferred it.

Always try and pick a different name for my characters, and Valkyrie's are 
always V-names....The use of
the name Verbose should give some indication over how many great-named Valks 
were slaughtered.

Anyway...highlights of my ascension.

* Finding a sink on level one, and still at the risk-taking stage, going for 
a ring but getting a pudding instead. Don't get too surrounded like usual(i 
think it's cheating that they can divide between your legs in corridors, 
grrr), and after killing about 7 of them the remaining 3 are trapped in a 
dead end curve and I've picked up shock resistance....

* ...Which came in insanely useful when I came across a bones file at 
Minetown. The shops were completely looted thanks to a polymorph spree the 
dead character had been on, said spree having come to an abrupt end when the 
Temple Priest had become a Blue Dragon. Luckily the dragon didn't seem to 
want to wander too far from the altar, so Verbose slowly wore it down with 
Excalibur, retreating where necessary and not bothered at all by 
dragonbreath and angry god.

* Finding on the body next to the dragon corpse two magic lamps(cursed of 
course), a +2 SDSM, THREE bags of holding, 3 luckstones, and the wand of 
polymorph which still had 4 charges.

* Used my two wishes for a CoMR(inadvertently iding the cursed cloak on the 
corpse...bugger) and speed boots.

* Things went fairly smoothly....sokoban completed but left the prize 
there(would have either way, for record it was my 5th BoH)

* No giant room, no fort....but I lost telepathy at one point, I think it 
was when I killed a vault guard...I left the other one(vault guard) alone 
after that.

* lost automatic searching at one point.....Tyr knows where?  Fought some 
gremlins down in Geh, but I think it was long gone already.

* found a magic marker, used it all up on enchant armor scrolls. Spent the 
dead polymorpher's cash at another altar I found in the main dungeon. 
Combined I managed to get an AC around -25.

* had lots of ring doubles, another sink helped me identify a bunch...found 
levitation just before Medusa.

* avoided the nasty things in the water, and crossed to take out Medusa 
easily(except for my telepathy loss, which would have made it easier).

* first big mistake at the Castle. I find I have nothing to let me get 
inside, so a blessed scroll of genocide(;) + ring of levitation nets me a 
way around. BUT I FORGET TO PUT THE STUPID RING ON!!! If I had drowned I 
would have been so mad. No oilskin bag for the entire game, so I lost a lot 
of potions and scrolls this way. Luckily, as stupid mistakes go, it could 
have been a lot worse. Wand of cancellation and BoH anyone? Boy have I been 
there.

* Wand of wishing has 3 charges, so I end up with 8 for the entire game. 
(kept the last one for an emergency, didn't need it). Frostbrand, a silver 
saber, Helm of brilliance, gloves of dexterity, t-shirt, a couple of magic 
markers, put my AC closer to -40....I'd been PLANNING on some spellcasting, 
but this never really panned out. I finally got Cone of Cold to 0% fail, 
then promptly forgot it. Plus my +7 elven daggers proved more-than-competent 
against any distant enemy. This did come in useful when I was portal hunting 
though. Would have wished for Grayswandir, but I was worried about my skill 
slots(needlessly as it worked out), having already filled long sword, 
dagger...and wanting to fill out twoweapon, saber, and attack spells. Among 
a lot of enchanting, made a couple more genocide scrolls and took care of L 
and h as well.

* Getting to Vlad's for the first time. :) Actually, somehow Asmodeus 
vanished while he was out of my line of sight, and I didn't find him til I 
was coming back with the amulet. Still a minor mystery how that happened, I 
did search for him, on the first level and the level above, since he'd 
disappeared near some up stairs.

* Getting overconfident, and choking to death on a wraith corpse. Thank you, 
Vlad's amulet of LS.

The rest was pretty uneventful, apart from being surprised by Asmodeus on 
the way back up. One level, I swear the WoY threw me back into about 5 
times. Dungeons of doom were quickly navigated, and my rusty ring of 
levitation saw me through the planes. Took the right turn at the Astral 
Plane, killed Famine twice with Orcus's wand, then Ascended.....thank you 
for not making me fight Death...he looked scary.

Just one question....how do you post all your ascension stats, or is that 
not doable with the windows version?

